solution:
The exponent \(30\) is twice \(15\), so write \(15^{30}=(15^2)^{15}\). This makes the numerator and denominator products of fifteen factors that can be paired:
\[
\frac{15^{30}}{45^{15}}
=\left(\frac{15^2}{45}\right)^{15}
=\left(\frac{225}{45}\right)^{15}
=\boxed{5^{15}}.
\]
The answer is choice \(\boxed{\text{E}}\).

